Use `terminated` for normal FCM delivery with the process absent. A `cold` row cannot use a custom trigger; `cold` is reserved for the runner’s URI-entry preparation.

```json
{
  "matrix_version": 2,
  "platform": "android",
  "target_kind": "android-emulator",
  "target_label": "test-android",
  "include_device_id": false,
  "app_id": "com.example.app",
  "timeout_seconds": 60,
  "context": {
    "build_mode": "debug",
    "entrypoint": "lib/main.dart",
    "data_source": "project notification fixture",
    "provider": "FCM test provider"
  },
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "terminated-fcm-notification-tap",
      "lifecycle": "terminated",
      "before": [
        {
          "name": "ensure registered and not force-stopped",
          "argv": ["tool/fcm-fixture", "prepare-registered-not-force-stopped"]
        }
      ],
      "precondition": [
        {
          "name": "verify app process absent",
          "argv": ["tool/assert-runtime-state", "process-absent"]
        }
      ],
      "trigger": {
        "name": "send, confirm receipt, and tap notification",
        "argv": ["tool/fcm-fixture", "send-confirm-receipt-and-tap", "order-42"]
      },
      "assert": [
        {
          "name": "opens order once",
          "argv": ["tool/assert-notification-route", "order-42", "1"]
        }
      ],
      "after": [
        {
          "name": "clear fixture state",
          "argv": ["tool/fcm-fixture", "clear"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "force-stop-fcm-does-not-deliver",
      "lifecycle": "force-stop",
      "before": [
        {
          "name": "ensure FCM registration",
          "argv": ["tool/fcm-fixture", "prepare-registered"]
        }
      ],
      "trigger": {
        "name": "send FCM and observe bounded delivery window",
        "argv": ["tool/fcm-fixture", "send-and-observe", "order-42", "30"]
      },
      "assert": [
        {
          "name": "no notification receipt or presentation while force-stopped",
          "argv": ["tool/assert-no-notification", "order-42"]
        }
      ],
      "after": [
        {
          "name": "clear fixture state",
          "argv": ["tool/fcm-fixture", "clear"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

The `terminated` row’s precondition must prove the process is absent, while its setup must also prove the registered app is no longer in Android’s force-stopped state. The `force-stop` lifecycle asks the runner to apply `am force-stop` before its trigger; there is no notification to tap if delivery is correctly suppressed.

If you also need to verify delivery after the user reopens the app, add that as a separate scenario—not as part of the force-stop assertion. Run the matrix dry run first and require a successful `planned` report before executing it.
